# The fields of kustomize's Kustomization type and of every type it holds, by the names kustomize
# reads them under: sigs.k8s.io/kustomize/api, types/*.go (Kustomization, ObjectMeta, Label, Patch,
# PatchArgs, Selector, Image, ReplacementField, Replacement, SourceSelector, TargetSelector,
# FieldOptions, Replica, Var, Target, FieldSelector, SortOptions, LegacySortOptions, ConfigMapArgs,
# SecretArgs, GeneratorArgs, KvPairSources, GeneratorOptions), with kyaml's resid.Gvk and
# resid.ResId inline where a type embeds them, and the keys of Kustomization.OpenAPI that
# kustomize reads (krusty/kustomizer.go). The two versions below hold the same types:
#
# flux: sigs.k8s.io/kustomize/api v0.21.2
# kustomize: v5.8.3 (sigs.k8s.io/kustomize/api v0.21.3)
# root: Kustomization
#
# flux builds with the api version its binary records; the kustomize binary records none, and its
# release names the version in kustomize/go.mod. tests/kubernetes-check.bats fails when either
# pinned tool moves to another version, until the fields are read again at the new one.
#
# Both read a kustomization with encoding/json, which matches a key to a field without regard to
# case, so the checks accept each field by exactly this name and refuse any other key at a typed
# position. One field a line: the type, the field, and what it holds:
#   value    a scalar, or a list of scalars, that names no file;
#   map      a map of strings, whose keys are data, not fields;
#   path     a file kustomize reads, or fetches;
#   paths    a list of files or directories kustomize reads, or remote sources it fetches;
#   dirs     a list of directories (Components) kustomize reads, or remote sources;
#   files    a list of KEY=FILE or FILE kustomize reads;
#   refused  generators, transformers and validators name plugin configurations, whose own fields
#            name more files, and Helm charts are inflated only with --enable-helm, which neither
#            Flux nor the checks give: the checks refuse a kustomization that sets one;
#   TYPE, []TYPE  an object of that type, or a list of them.
